From 60cf4dd015380f71b372179eca61f544a2beb56d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 04:00:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: add native Linux journal output without libsystemd

Encode PRIORITY, MESSAGE, CODE_* and LOTUS_* fields with native binary framing. Connect to the journal socket only on Linux; preserve readable console/callback output and an optional generic JSON file. Oversize entries use a fully sealed memfd, and socket replacement reconnects. Startup fails on a missing socket; later send failures use stderr and an explicit counter.

Validated 34 native logging/event cases and feature_logging on macOS. Actual JournalSink compiled with GCC14 on Linux aarch64; maintained transport test body passes using an assertion shim. A real isolated systemd 257 journal preserved multiline/NUL and 2 MB records. Full Linux daemon/Boost suite was not run.

(cherry picked from commit 395cc1180700b82515f75228cdf2a4e287e04843)

